# --- Vendored engines -------------------------------------------------------
# Everything above targets the pokeemerald decomp tree at the repo root. Those
# patterns (*.bat, *.js, *.a, *.map, build/, ...) are far too broad for the
# vendored engine subtrees and would silently swallow real upstream sources
# (Play-Windows.bat, gradlew.bat, test/*.test.js, ...). Opt the subtree out
# here; engines/gen1recomp/.gitignore is deeper, so its own rules still take
# precedence and its build artifacts stay ignored.
!engines/gen1recomp/**

# apps/ is our own code, not decomp build output. The *.js rule above is for
# generated tools; it would silently drop apps/realms/src/*.js (it did once).
!/apps/**/*.js

# ...but never absorb the two large third-party trees that upstream tracks and
# we deliberately do not vendor (~186 MB of LOVE/SDL2/LuaJIT/oboe sources and
# prebuilt ANGLE/SDL2/OpenAL DLLs). engines/restore-gen1recomp-blobs.sh drops
# them back in for Android/UWP builds; these rules keep that from dirtying the
# working tree or getting committed. See engines/VENDOR.md.
engines/gen1recomp/mobile/android/love/src/jni/
engines/gen1recomp/ports/uwp/third_party/
